# Research campaign v3

Public entry point: `run.py prepare|dry-run|submit|worker|status|closeout`.
Use the private WORK vLLM-cu129 Python. Scientific stages require a Slurm step;
`prepare`, `dry-run`, `submit`, and bounded `status` are orchestration commands.
`worker` accepts `--stage`, `--model`, `--threshold-index`, `--shard-index`, or an
immutable `--card`; array tasks map through the card's `array_cards` table.

The user-authorized launcher registers the entire finite graph, submits source
resolution and the October 15 snapshot, then accepts a held controller plus two
failure owners before releasing the deepest owner first. Every submission is
journaled before `sbatch`, verified by job ID and exact comment, and reconciled
after an ambiguous response. A started scientific unit is never redrawn. One
replacement is allowed only with zero-runtime, unset-Start, no-unit-start proof.
Ordinary controllers request two CPUs, 4 GiB and 60 minutes. Frozen expert masks
are referenced once instead of repeated throughout execution tables. The final
failure owner retains four CPUs, 24 GiB and 180 minutes for terminal exports.
Admission jointly checks serial running/submitted jobs, CPUs and memory, and
verifies requested or allocated billing resources after every acceptance.

`prepare --resume-from report/research-campaign-v2-20261009-r1` binds compatible
completed evidence by reference through cycle-checked v2/v1 ancestry. It preserves
failed receipts and separately reuses router banks and qualified REAP components.
Replacement norm measurements identify the original assignment and defect.
Before dispatch ownership changes, all new operational owners are
accepted and verified; the old journal is reconciled under its controller lock.
Only reconciled pending operational owners are retired. Scientific jobs continue.
`status` is compact; `--detailed` includes the complete receipts.

Read the campaign's `CAMPAIGN.json`, `PROTOCOL.json`, `GRAPH.json`, `LAUNCH.json`,
`REUSE.json`, stage receipts, and admission reports. Later configurations, masks,
task tables and measured role prices are immutable. Native sources are read in
place; original controllers and scientific implementations are preserved.
Do not edit bound source files after launch. Repairs require a fresh campaign
binding and exact reconciliation; ordinary progression needs no assistant process.

The code, tests, runtime dependencies, protocol and finite dependency graph are
sealed together. The fixed pruning roster is 420 questions/400 families; the
causal roster is 131 questions/129 families. No unavailable prefix is replaced.
Numeric normalization preserves unavailable values and reasons through inherited
Parquet ingestion, aggregation, hashing and strict JSON publication.

Each original capture is verified once per extraction. Indexed, lossless arrays
retain labelled-token selected IDs by layer, token position and class/segment
ownership. Occupancy and turnover use that same pass. Pair calculations read
only two layers and hold one pair's dense discovery accumulators. Nominations,
family sufficient statistics, support and resampling identities are durable.
Only one model's temporary cache is active, and only v3-owned intermediates are
retired after dependent evidence and checksums are durable. The initial retained
CPU role uses four CPUs/24 GiB/180 minutes per model, at most 84 local hours or
105 with margin. Remaining shard sizes and admission use measured extraction,
pair/bootstrap time, peak RSS and output bytes. The historical 981-worker-hour
extrapolation is not a launch forecast.

The pipeline joins card-v3 sources and the original 1,486-family fold universe,
derives absent saved-data summaries, measures absent native REAP/router quantities
on original saved sequences, freezes discovery-only configurations/masks, qualifies
physical loading and within-execution interventions, retains original-role prices,
and admits the complete residual production workload automatically. Normal QoS,
account `iscrc_miosr`, GPU partition `boost_usr_prod`, and bounded serial partition
`lrd_all_serial` are rechecked with exact Lustre project quota. Spending authority
is at most 42,050 local hours, reduced by expenditure/reservations, with 25% cost
margin, a 10 GiB scientific-output reserve, and explicit terminal infeasibility.

Signed multi-expert actions preserve native selection, correction bias, k, scales
and shared experts. Saved prefixes retain cumulative generation allowances and
completion penalty history. Pruning physically removes storage, including GPT's
unequal MXFP4 retained counts, under a fixed qualified KV capacity per model.
Memory curves use actual process residence from the common full-context
qualification fixture for each retained-count shape; ordinary generation
residence is exported separately so workspace history does not bias comparisons.
Original seven-class rendering/parsing is pinned in a private CPU dependency
closure; speculative acceleration is disabled and disclosed. Invalid or truncated
labels, conflicting original contexts, capped outputs and scientific failures are
retained without redraws. Strict accuracy is separate from semantic unknown bounds
and historical adjudication; the old candidate/J1 workflow is not restarted.

`PRE_PRODUCTION_DECISION.json` binds repaired evidence, operator limitations,
realized support, complete measured residual cost, peak storage and execution
projections before production admission. Queue uncertainty stays separate.
The handoff bound derives from registered shards, aggregation, permitted recovery
and report owners. Capacity deferrals wait on owned events. Shared implementation
failures block dependent dispatch immediately; model/method limitations retain
independent cells. Accounting recursively deduplicates original Slurm task IDs.

Final data, tables, figures, provenance and feasibility reports live under `output/`.
The October 15 report lives under `snapshots/2026-10-15/`. Root `REPORT_COMPLETE.json`
does not imply `SCIENCE_COMPLETE.json` is true. Support and 10,000-draw paired
whole-family simultaneous intervals condition on frozen selections. Coordination
predeclares linear and log-odds subpanels with alpha 0.025 each and the same paired
draws, retaining simultaneous 95% coverage across the original panel. Supported
linear statistics remain estimable beside unsupported odds; undefined draws are
never dropped. Degenerate and unsupported intervals are unavailable; selection
stability is reported separately. Native accuracy joins each exact original draw.
Full-A token ownership is recovered from original labels and trace offsets and
checked against all nine saved class counts. This cache does not change enrollment.
One initial replicate has no run-to-run SD. Paired pruned-minus-native and
same-budget method differences include token cost and asymmetric unknown bounds.
Causal target-minus-native/random responses remain separate by class, depth,
sign and configuration. PDF/SVG figures and machine-readable plotting tables
bind source hashes. Referenced masks use the validated resolver; missing runtime,
physical count, full-context or fixed-KV qualification means unavailable memory.
Empty memory panels establish no savings. V3 generated paper exhibits and wiki
status update from observed evidence while historical findings remain preserved.
Intervals crossing zero do not establish equivalence.

Bounded local verification:

```sh
PYTHONPATH=src:scripts/experimental_resume python -B -m unittest discover -s tests/research_campaign_v3 -v
```

GPU qualification starts with Qwen3-30B's genuinely missing two-GPU pilot, then
replaces only four defective REAP components. Six valid router banks and the
qualified Qwen3.5/Qwen3.6 components are reused. At most five allocations use
two GPUs/16 CPUs/120 minutes each (160 local hours, 200 with margin, subject
to verified billing). Scoped native pre-reduction Marlin/Triton adapters and
GPT's available unfused measurement path preserve native selection, quantized
weights, biases, activation, scaling and TP reduction. Actual native routing
weights qualify reconstruction; a separate invocation with unit weights obtains
unweighted expert outputs. The tolerance remains unchanged. Unsupported backends
receive explicit method/model limitations; independently qualified methods and
router banks stay usable. Hooks and adapters restore after success or failure.
Later waves have separate complete-residual admission.
Qualification runs inside the automatically protected graph. It tests native
selector fidelity, both action signs, multiple IDs, pulse boundaries, closure,
fixed full-context KV capacity, compact/full-resident masked equivalence and actual
storage release. It does not require sampled cross-run replay.
